        "label": "Mars orbit insertion",
        "description": "27-minute main-engine burn on 2021-02-09 captured Hope into a 22,000 × 43,000 km orbit. Hope is the first Mars mission to study the planet's lower atmosphere + weather + dust storms from a high-altitude 55-hour orbit — a vantage point that complements the lower-orbit science missions (MAVEN, TGO) it shares the Mars system with."
